  taxonomic_groups[19]{id,label,common_traits,notes}:
    group_small_mammals,Small Mammals,"Small rodents, shrews, and other small mammals; important prey for raptors and predators; seed dispersers","Rodentia, Soricomorpha; includes rabbits, rats, mice, shrews, moles"
    group_predatory_mammals,Predatory Mammals,Carnivorous and omnivorous mammals; predators of small animals; keystone species in many ecosystems,"Carnivora; includes mustelids, felids, canids, ursids"
    group_ground_nesting_birds,Ground-Nesting Birds,Birds that nest on the ground; grassland and scrubland specialists; depend on open habitats,"Various orders; includes quail, meadowlarks, sparrows, nighthawks"
    group_raptors,Raptors,"Birds of prey; apex and secondary predators; cavity nesters or open nesters; hunt birds, mammals, and reptiles","Falconiformes, Strigiformes; eagles, hawks, owls, falcons, kites"
    group_other_birds,Other Birds,Diverse songbirds and other species; varied diets and habitats; important seed dispersers and insect controllers,"Various orders; includes woodpeckers, corvids, warblers, kingfishers, wrens"
    group_lizards,Lizards,Scaled reptiles; mostly insectivorous; diurnal and cryptic species; threatened by habitat loss,"Squamata; includes skinks, anoles, glass lizards, fence lizards"
    group_snakes,Snakes,Legless reptiles; ophiophagous and rodent hunters; venomous and non-venomous species; important predators,"Squamata, Serpentes; includes rattlesnakes, kingsnakes, water snakes, rat snakes"
    group_other_reptiles,Turtles and Other Reptiles,Armored reptiles; aquatic and terrestrial species; long-lived; keystone ecosystem engineers,"Testudines; includes box turtles, terapins, cooters, mud turtles, snappers"
    group_frogs_toads,Frogs & Toads,Amphibians with aquatic larval stage; bioindicators of water quality; chorus callers; varied habitat preferences,"Order Anura; families Ranidae, Hylidae, Bufonidae"
    group_salamanders,Salamanders,Aquatic and terrestrial amphibians; lungless and lunged species; moisture-dependent; important in food webs,"Order Caudata; families Ambystomatidae, Plethodontidae, Proteidae"
    group_insects,Insects,"Arthropods with six legs; include herbivores, predators, pollinators, and decomposers; enormous diversity","Class Insecta; includes beetles, butterflies, ants, wasps, dragonflies, grasshoppers"
    group_spiders_arachnids,Spiders & Arachnids,Eight-legged arthropods; predators of insects and small animals; venomous; web-builders and hunters,Class Arachnida; orders Araneae and Scorpiones
    group_pine_trees,Pine Trees,Coniferous trees; fire-adapted in longleaf pine ecosystem; provide habitat structure; needle-bearing evergreens,"Genus Pinus; includes Longleaf, Slash, Loblolly, and Sand Pine"
    group_hardwoods,Hardwood Trees,Broad-leaved trees; deciduous and evergreen species; important in forest structure; diverse wildlife habitat,"Various families; includes magnolia, sweetgum, maple, and cypress species"
    group_conifers,Coniferous Trees,Needle or scale-bearing evergreens; adapted to various environments; provide year-round structure,"Includes pine, cedar, and cypress families"
    group_grasses,Grasses,Herbaceous plants; fire-adapted; foundational to grassland and longleaf pine ecosystems,Family Poaceae; includes wiregrass and dropseed species essential to ecosystem structure
    group_shrubs,Shrubs & Understory Plants,Woody and herbaceous shrubs; berry and fruit producers; essential wildlife food sources; understory dominants,"Various families; includes palmetto, blueberry, beautyberry, and other mast-producing species"
    group_other_invertebrates,Other Invertebrates,"Diverse arthropods, mollusks, and worms; essential decomposers and food web members; soil and detritus processors","Includes centipedes, millipedes, earthworms, snails, slugs, crustaceans, springtails"
    group_fungi,Fungi,Decomposers and mycorrhizal partners; form symbiotic relationships with plant roots; essential nutrient cyclers; diverse morphology,"Kingdom Fungi; includes mushrooms, truffles, polypores, and other fungal fruiting bodies"